      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_tinwini_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species of spiny eel has been described scientifically quite recently. It is a close relative of the common spiny eel of Asia, Mastacembelus armatus. Like that species, M. tinwini reaches a length of about 40 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/mastacembelus_tinwini_en/",
      "html": "<p>Other fish are ignored if they are large enough, but small tankmates are taken for food.</p>"
    }
